    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploitation of secondary pitching matchups, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (77.19) and **Christian Yelich** (71.63). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** represents our highest ceiling play, as the matchup against Erick Fedde allows us to leverage his elite sprint speed; his 19% boost from the SP skill profile and the advantage of Fedde\u2019s slower delivery to the plate make him an essential anchor in this lineup despite the gusty wind conditions. **Christian Yelich** follows closely behind, benefiting significantly from a dynamic platoon edge against Bailey Ober. While **Junior Caminero** (63.35) and **Carson Benge** (63.27) round out the top of our high-efficiency starts, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite the tough matchup against Nathan Eovaldi; his elite 0.425 xwOBA provides a floor that the optimizer simply cannot ignore, even when facing high-end strikeout arms.\n\nNavigating the rotation proved difficult at the fringes, specifically with **Hyeseong Kim** (50.35) narrowly missing the cut. While **Hyeseong Kim** presents a strong profile, his projected #9 spot in the order acted as a significant anchor on his daily efficiency score, causing the optimizer to prefer the higher lineup placement of **Gary Sanchez** (50.69) and **Trea Turner** (49.86), despite the latter\u2019s daunting matchup against Paul Skenes. We must remain vigilant regarding the risk associated with the Skenes start; both **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** (47.62) take significant hits to their projected output due to his elite pitch modeling. Furthermore, investors should note that the lineup for **Gary Sanchez** is still pending, and should he be dropped down or rested, we will need to pivot to the bench to preserve our game cap efficiency. We are currently holding **Zac Veen** and **Caleb Durbin** in reserve, keeping a close eye on roster health as we manage our remaining games for the week.",
